invariant: INV-44
file: p384_wide_point.c
catches: p384_equiv_test
reason: the addition doubles its left operand for a point and its
  negative, where the sum is infinity. With the key -G and scalars
  that differ by five, each digit of the second scalar adds the
  negative of what the first just added. bin/p384_equiv_test verifies
  that signature and wants 1.

--- old
        if (p384_wide_is_zero(rr)) {
            point_double(o, a);
        } else {
            memset(o, 0, sizeof *o);
        }
--- new
        if (p384_wide_is_zero(rr)) {
            point_double(o, a);
        } else {
            point_double(o, a);
        }
